    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="11" relname="span">I was just on the site www.usability.gov which is maintained by the US Department of Health and Human Services.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="15" relname="span">The site is wonderful.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="evidence">It explains usability and then gets into much detail.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="16" relname="span">The main page is displayed very friendly and easy to read.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="evidence">Each topic is grouped and linked to another page that explains the topic is much more detail.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="17" relname="span">There are quite alot of usability resources here</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="14" relname="span">- everything from planning usable web sites to internet survey results</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="7" relname="summary">- it's all here.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="11" relname="background">I'm sure Professor P11 has seen this one already.</segment>
